1
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:03,247
<i>Kazumi, how are you?</i>

2
00:00:03,247 --> 00:00:05,033
<i>Are you eating properly?</i>

3
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:06,607
<i>Yeah, I am.</i>

4
00:00:06,607 --> 00:00:11,490
<i>But nothing beats meals with you.</i>

5
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:14,224
<i>I miss your rolled dashi omelets.</i>

6
00:00:14,224 --> 00:00:15,858
<i>That stuff is the best.</i>

7
00:00:15,858 --> 00:00:18,405
- Good work today.
- Nice to meet you.

8
00:00:18,405 --> 00:00:19,432
My name is...

9
00:00:19,432 --> 00:00:21,944
<i>You're exaggerating.</i>

10
00:00:21,944 --> 00:00:25,704
<i>Oh, I found a great place near the office.</i>

11
00:00:25,704 --> 00:00:27,582
<i>Let's go together next time.</i>

12
00:00:27,582 --> 00:00:30,877
<i>Sounds good. I'm looking forward to it.</i>

13
00:00:30,877 --> 00:00:32,685
<i>How's work?</i>

14
00:00:32,685 --> 00:00:34,065
<i>Going well.</i>

15
00:00:34,065 --> 00:00:37,105
<i>Everyone's nice, so I feel relieved.</i>

16
00:00:37,105 --> 00:00:38,782
<i>And you?</i>

17
00:00:38,782 --> 00:00:40,797
<i>Yeah, it's going well.</i>

18
00:00:40,797 --> 00:00:44,931
<i>The other day, Nihei and I
nailed a presentation together.</i>

19
00:00:45,568 --> 00:00:48,430
<i>I'm glad you two are doing well.</i>

20
00:00:51,537 --> 00:00:56,353
Doesn't this deviate
from what I proposed last time?

21
00:00:56,353 --> 00:00:57,693
Huh?

22
00:00:58,744 --> 00:01:01,830
We want the older demographic to feel at ease

23
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:06,035
while also appealing to younger audiences.

24
00:01:07,955 --> 00:01:09,967
I sincerely apologize.

25
00:01:09,967 --> 00:01:11,767
We're very sorry.

26
00:01:11,767 --> 00:01:13,553
Let's send those documents first.

27
00:01:13,553 --> 00:01:17,008
<i>Let us handle things over here.</i>

28
00:01:17,008 --> 00:01:19,607
<i>Oh, that's reassuring.</i>

29
00:01:19,607 --> 00:01:24,913
<i>Well, I can't be as smooth as you,
but I'll do my best.</i>

30
00:01:24,913 --> 00:01:27,098
<i>So you do your best too.</i>

31
00:01:27,098 --> 00:01:31,408
<i>Okay, just do things
how you'd normally do them.</i>

32
00:01:31,408 --> 00:01:35,189
<i>Thanks. Everyone's been supporting me too.</i>

33
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:38,319
I have a good feeling about this one.

34
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:41,639
Maybe even Hojo would accept it
without any edits.

35
00:01:41,639 --> 00:01:43,526
That's expecting a bit much.

36
00:01:43,526 --> 00:01:46,037
But some praise would be nice, huh?

37
00:01:46,037 --> 00:01:47,627
Okay, everyone!

38
00:01:47,627 --> 00:01:49,950
Let's take a coffee break!

39
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:52,758
Nice! That's Shibasaki for you!

40
00:01:52,758 --> 00:01:55,357
Thank you!

41
00:01:55,357 --> 00:01:58,679
Let's take a picture and send it to Hojo.

42
00:01:58,679 --> 00:02:03,561
Here we go! Say cheese!

43
00:02:03,561 --> 00:02:06,929
<i>Here's a photo we took today. Take a look.</i>

44
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:17,546
Yeah, feels like a solid team.

45
00:02:17,546 --> 00:02:19,046
<i>Right?</i>

46
00:02:19,046 --> 00:02:23,579
<i>And Nihei's amazing.
His ideas just keep coming.</i>

47
00:02:23,579 --> 00:02:26,428
<i>Even the chief's looking forward to them.</i>

48
00:02:26,428 --> 00:02:27,978
I see.

49
00:02:29,283 --> 00:02:30,636
<i>I should get back.</i>

50
00:02:30,636 --> 00:02:32,784
<i>All right, keep it up!</i>

51
00:02:32,784 --> 00:02:35,083
Yeah, you too.

52
00:03:31,446 --> 00:03:35,521
Yanami still wasn't satisfied today.

53
00:03:35,521 --> 00:03:37,592
But I was so confident.

54
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:41,312
They're really picky, huh?

55
00:03:41,312 --> 00:03:44,992
Well, it just means
they have high expectations of us.

56
00:03:44,992 --> 00:03:46,626
Yeah, I guess.

57
00:03:46,626 --> 00:03:49,369
Still, it'd be easier to move forward

58
00:03:49,369 --> 00:03:51,465
if the back-and-forth were a bit smoother.

59
00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:54,217
But I feel like we haven't fully drawn out

60
00:03:54,217 --> 00:03:57,433
what Yanami is really thinking yet.

61
00:03:57,433 --> 00:04:01,784
No, that's supposed to be my job.

62
00:04:01,784 --> 00:04:04,491
Maybe I still haven't earned their trust.

63
00:04:04,491 --> 00:04:05,918
That's not true.

64
00:04:05,918 --> 00:04:10,223
You're doing plenty
to try and meet Yanami's expectations.

65
00:04:10,223 --> 00:04:12,209
Thanks.

66
00:04:12,209 --> 00:04:17,341
But when I think about
how Hojo handles this every time,

67
00:04:17,341 --> 00:04:19,580
it's impressive.

68
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:22,190
He's a genius at communicating.

69
00:04:22,812 --> 00:04:26,110
We gotta work hard so we don't fall behind.

70
00:04:29,526 --> 00:04:31,115
What's wrong?

71
00:04:33,834 --> 00:04:35,619
Shibasaki.

72
00:04:36,739 --> 00:04:38,613
It's been a week.

73
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:42,729
Huh? What do you mean?

74
00:04:42,729 --> 00:04:46,840
The thing I asked you earlier.
Can you give me an answer?

75
00:04:48,433 --> 00:04:51,133
It's because I like you.

76
00:04:51,133 --> 00:04:54,305
- Huh?
- You don't have to answer now.

77
00:04:55,725 --> 00:04:58,713
<i>I thought that was a joke...</i>

78
00:05:03,483 --> 00:05:06,514
<i>I guess it wasn't.</i>

79
00:05:07,588 --> 00:05:11,084
<i>I need to give him a proper answer.</i>

80
00:05:14,084 --> 00:05:15,625
I'm sorry.

81
00:05:17,009 --> 00:05:21,791
I've never seen you that way, Nihei.

82
00:05:23,512 --> 00:05:25,628
And that won't change?

83
00:05:26,988 --> 00:05:29,214
Yeah, I don't think so.

84
00:05:29,214 --> 00:05:30,568
That was blunt.

85
00:05:30,568 --> 00:05:34,166
I thought being vague
would be more disrespectful.

86
00:05:34,951 --> 00:05:40,194
Besides, I have someone
I really like right now.

87
00:05:40,194 --> 00:05:43,729
So I can't think about anyone else.

88
00:05:44,832 --> 00:05:46,152
It's Hojo, right?

89
00:05:46,152 --> 00:05:48,458
Huh? No, that's not...

90
00:05:48,458 --> 00:05:50,389
Shibasaki, it's obvious.

91
00:05:50,389 --> 00:05:52,706
I know you're together.

92
00:05:56,534 --> 00:05:58,394
I see.

93
00:06:02,618 --> 00:06:05,581
Am I not good enough?

94
00:06:06,464 --> 00:06:10,308
It's not that you're not good enough, but...

95
00:06:10,308 --> 00:06:12,634
Why is it Hojo?

96
00:06:18,898 --> 00:06:24,591
When I was little,
my mother got sick and passed away.

97
00:06:25,739 --> 00:06:29,067
So my father raised me.

98
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:33,559
Kazumi wasn't like other people.

99
00:06:34,274 --> 00:06:37,099
Even when he found out,

100
00:06:37,099 --> 00:06:40,285
he never looked at me with sympathy or pity.

101
00:06:42,207 --> 00:06:47,261
After my mom died,
lots of people felt sorry for me.

102
00:06:47,261 --> 00:06:50,718
"Poor thing". "That must be tough".

103
00:06:50,718 --> 00:06:53,203
Everyone was kind.

104
00:06:54,024 --> 00:07:00,265
But being told that made me feel miserable.

105
00:07:02,861 --> 00:07:05,253
Is that how you feel too?

106
00:07:06,714 --> 00:07:11,988
Sorry, for a second, I did feel sad for you.

107
00:07:11,988 --> 00:07:14,715
No, it's okay, it's okay.

108
00:07:14,715 --> 00:07:19,722
But I didn't want to feel sorry for myself,

109
00:07:19,722 --> 00:07:22,242
and I didn't want pity.

110
00:07:22,242 --> 00:07:25,449
So I'd force myself to act okay.

111
00:07:26,356 --> 00:07:30,211
That was around when I met Kazumi.

112
00:07:31,981 --> 00:07:37,814
My dad didn't want the other kids
to feel sorry for me,

113
00:07:37,814 --> 00:07:41,520
so he always did everything he could for me.

114
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:45,393
That's why I never felt sad.

115
00:07:47,483 --> 00:07:49,792
I bet she was a wonderful mother.

116
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:51,755
Huh?

117
00:07:52,508 --> 00:07:56,320
I mean, look at how amazing you turned out.

118
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:02,557
I knew it.

119
00:08:03,493 --> 00:08:05,797
You're a bit strange, Kazumi.

120
00:08:05,797 --> 00:08:08,416
Huh? You think?

121
00:08:09,563 --> 00:08:13,853
He said she's a good mother,
and that's why she found a good father.

122
00:08:13,853 --> 00:08:17,614
Everyone thinks talking about my mom
is taboo,

123
00:08:17,614 --> 00:08:22,168
but it felt like he acknowledged
that my mother existed.

124
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:25,843
That made me so happy.

125
00:08:25,843 --> 00:08:30,026
Because to me, she was the best mother.

126
00:08:30,026 --> 00:08:31,773
I see.

127
00:08:32,536 --> 00:08:34,977
Sorry, I talked for too long.

128
00:08:34,977 --> 00:08:36,568
Not at all.

129
00:08:38,294 --> 00:08:40,906
Can I ask you something then?

130
00:08:41,882 --> 00:08:43,866
Why me?

131
00:08:43,866 --> 00:08:45,292
Huh?

132
00:08:48,230 --> 00:08:49,589
Well...

133
00:08:53,224 --> 00:08:55,589
When I first joined the company,

134
00:08:55,589 --> 00:08:59,088
the vibe in our department
was terrible, right?

135
00:08:59,754 --> 00:09:03,011
That manager got demoted, right?

136
00:09:03,638 --> 00:09:08,514
I was being targeted and bullied
because of how I am,

137
00:09:08,514 --> 00:09:12,468
but do you remember
how you stood up for me?

138
00:09:13,074 --> 00:09:17,652
"That's not management.
Give him clear instructions", you said.

139
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,655
I vaguely remember that.

140
00:09:23,786 --> 00:09:27,116
You hold back your own struggles,

141
00:09:27,116 --> 00:09:30,152
but you can get that angry for someone else.

142
00:09:31,836 --> 00:09:34,251
I thought that was admirable.

143
00:09:35,650 --> 00:09:38,067
You think so?

144
00:09:38,067 --> 00:09:39,828
Yeah.

145
00:09:42,327 --> 00:09:46,430
That's when I fell for you.

146
00:10:10,366 --> 00:10:11,819
I'm...

147
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:15,155
I'm not giving up.

148
00:10:16,684 --> 00:10:18,588
I'm serious about this.

149
00:10:37,432 --> 00:10:41,527
<i>Nihei was serious after all.</i>

150
00:10:43,271 --> 00:10:47,734
<i>It's not like
my feelings wavered or anything.</i>

151
00:10:47,734 --> 00:10:53,247
<i>But it did make me happy.</i>

152
00:10:56,993 --> 00:11:00,382
[Kazumi Hojo]

153
00:11:04,195 --> 00:11:06,969
I kind of wanted to talk to him.

154
00:11:08,413 --> 00:11:12,089
No, I gotta focus on work!

155
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:16,562
I have to support Kazumi properly.

156
00:11:23,451 --> 00:11:27,297
This won't do. It could damage our brand.

157
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:33,776
But you mentioned reaching younger
demographics was your top priority.

158
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:36,689
That doesn't mean you can damage our brand.

159
00:11:36,689 --> 00:11:39,790
This is totally different.

160
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:42,333
Do you have another idea?

161
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:44,039
You do, don't you?

162
00:11:47,822 --> 00:11:49,568
I'm sorry.

163
00:11:50,379 --> 00:11:51,409
No, wait a second.

164
00:11:51,409 --> 00:11:55,114
You agreed that we could push the envelope
to this extent.

165
00:11:55,114 --> 00:11:56,964
It's written down.

166
00:11:56,964 --> 00:12:00,193
Yes, but it looks different
when you actually create it.

167
00:12:00,193 --> 00:12:05,240
That's exactly why you should be
bringing alternatives, am I wrong?

168
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,813
I understand what you're saying.

169
00:12:06,813 --> 00:12:10,305
But could you also be clearer
about the direction you want?

170
00:12:10,305 --> 00:12:11,920
We're just going in circles.

171
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:13,633
Nihei!

172
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:16,043
Are you saying this is our fault?

173
00:12:16,043 --> 00:12:18,149
I apologize. I'll prepare it right away.

174
00:12:18,149 --> 00:12:20,362
That won't be necessary.

175
00:12:20,362 --> 00:12:23,699
Let's just forget about this.

176
00:12:23,699 --> 00:12:26,252
Sorry, but Shibasaki...

177
00:12:26,252 --> 00:12:28,311
you're not up to this.

178
00:12:28,311 --> 00:12:33,176
I'll contact your office
to get Hojo back on this project.

179
00:12:33,176 --> 00:12:35,365
- That's not fair!
- Wait.

180
00:12:36,539 --> 00:12:39,717
Please give me another chance.

181
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:41,397
Please.

182
00:12:49,173 --> 00:12:51,307
Fine.

183
00:12:51,307 --> 00:12:52,629
One o'clock, in two days.

184
00:12:52,629 --> 00:12:55,181
That's your final deadline.

185
00:12:55,181 --> 00:13:01,959
I trust you'll bring us something
we'll be satisfied with this time.

186
00:13:01,959 --> 00:13:03,794
Thank you very much.

187
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:14,735
[Vextos]

188
00:13:16,896 --> 00:13:18,973
I'm sorry.

189
00:13:22,094 --> 00:13:24,127
I get how you feel.

190
00:13:24,127 --> 00:13:26,418
I was mad too.

191
00:13:26,418 --> 00:13:27,713
But...

192
00:13:27,713 --> 00:13:32,933
being blunt isn't always right,
and there's a way to say things.

193
00:13:32,933 --> 00:13:36,201
I let my anger get the best of me.

194
00:13:40,495 --> 00:13:43,078
[Kazumi Hojo]

195
00:13:46,184 --> 00:13:47,399
One second.

196
00:13:47,399 --> 00:13:48,631
Okay.

197
00:13:50,472 --> 00:13:53,385
Hello, this is Shibasaki.

198
00:13:53,385 --> 00:13:57,195
Oh, sorry, are you still at the office?

199
00:13:57,195 --> 00:13:58,956
Should I call back?

200
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:02,469
Did someone tell you?

201
00:14:02,469 --> 00:14:05,161
Huh? Did something happen?

202
00:14:07,987 --> 00:14:10,193
Shibasaki. Nihei.

203
00:14:10,193 --> 00:14:13,096
<i>The chief wants to hear what happened.</i>

204
00:14:13,096 --> 00:14:15,570
<i>Got it.</i>

205
00:14:15,570 --> 00:14:18,926
<i>Sorry, I've got to go.</i>

206
00:14:18,926 --> 00:14:20,483
Are you okay?

207
00:14:20,483 --> 00:14:24,086
<i>Yeah, it's fine. Don't worry.</i>

208
00:14:24,086 --> 00:14:26,365
I see.

209
00:14:27,097 --> 00:14:29,327
I'll be back tomorrow.

210
00:14:30,155 --> 00:14:33,195
Okay. I'm looking forward to it.

211
00:14:33,195 --> 00:14:34,635
Bye.

212
00:15:02,856 --> 00:15:06,740
I'm home. Sorry I'm late.

213
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,050
Welcome back.

214
00:15:08,050 --> 00:15:09,777
Must've been a long day.

215
00:15:09,777 --> 00:15:12,218
I made dinner.

216
00:15:12,218 --> 00:15:16,486
Thanks! Yet you're the one who's busier.

217
00:15:16,486 --> 00:15:19,400
Two weeks felt so long.

218
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:21,673
I missed you too.

219
00:15:21,673 --> 00:15:22,839
Let me help then.

220
00:15:22,839 --> 00:15:24,056
Okay, thanks.

221
00:15:24,056 --> 00:15:26,311
I'll grab the eggs.

222
00:15:33,630 --> 00:15:35,435
Did you smoke?

223
00:15:36,216 --> 00:15:38,310
No, I didn't.

224
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:40,887
A lot of people smoke over there,

225
00:15:40,887 --> 00:15:43,651
so the smoking area was like a meeting room.

226
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:47,093
- Does it smell?
- No, I was just curious.

227
00:15:47,093 --> 00:15:48,430
Nothing happened.

228
00:15:48,430 --> 00:15:52,804
Anyway, I bought a lot of souvenirs.

229
00:15:52,804 --> 00:15:56,716
Look, I brought Hakata Torimon.

230
00:15:58,878 --> 00:16:00,805
I missed you.

231
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:32,791
<i>Being held by you, Kazumi...</i>

232
00:16:34,970 --> 00:16:36,674
<i>It calms me.</i>

233
00:16:37,855 --> 00:16:43,082
<i>I wish this moment could last forever.</i>

234
00:16:43,082 --> 00:16:47,185
<i>It feels like we're melting together,</i>

235
00:16:47,185 --> 00:16:50,520
<i>and it's just unbelievably comforting.</i>

236
00:16:56,376 --> 00:17:00,024
So, how was Fukuoka?

237
00:17:00,024 --> 00:17:01,714
Ate any good food?

238
00:17:01,714 --> 00:17:04,347
Didn't have much time, honestly.

239
00:17:04,347 --> 00:17:06,847
I was working pretty late most nights.

240
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:09,046
I did have Hakata ramen though.

241
00:17:09,779 --> 00:17:11,956
How nice.

242
00:17:11,956 --> 00:17:13,389
And you?

243
00:17:13,389 --> 00:17:15,536
How's the Yanami project?

244
00:17:15,536 --> 00:17:18,590
Yeah, it's going well.

245
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:20,596
Good, I'm glad.

246
00:17:20,596 --> 00:17:23,191
Yanami is pretty particular,

247
00:17:23,191 --> 00:17:27,337
and they sometimes change their mind
at the last minute, so I was worried.

248
00:17:27,965 --> 00:17:30,168
I'm impressed.

249
00:17:37,408 --> 00:17:39,152
Did something happen?

250
00:17:39,810 --> 00:17:43,115
No, nothing.

251
00:17:46,099 --> 00:17:47,905
Can I ask you something?

252
00:17:47,905 --> 00:17:50,511
Yeah, what?

253
00:17:50,511 --> 00:17:55,877
When we were on the phone yesterday,
the chief called you two over, right?

254
00:17:55,877 --> 00:17:57,588
What happened?

255
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,014
Right.

256
00:18:09,728 --> 00:18:15,122
Well, actually,
we had an argument with Yanami.

257
00:18:15,122 --> 00:18:16,502
Huh?

258
00:18:16,502 --> 00:18:19,672
Nihei talked back a little.

259
00:18:19,672 --> 00:18:22,076
That made Yanami angry,

260
00:18:22,076 --> 00:18:26,033
and they said to just forget the whole thing.

261
00:18:33,145 --> 00:18:36,709
I understand there are circumstances,

262
00:18:36,709 --> 00:18:39,529
but if Nihei said something rude
and provoked them,

263
00:18:39,529 --> 00:18:41,927
then he should apologize.

264
00:18:41,927 --> 00:18:44,964
But I'm the one in charge,
so I should properly...

265
00:18:44,964 --> 00:18:47,734
Making it clear
that it was Nihei's responsibility

266
00:18:47,734 --> 00:18:49,958
is better for his sake.

267
00:18:49,958 --> 00:18:53,078
But I was pretty upset too, you know.

268
00:18:53,078 --> 00:18:56,729
- So it wasn't all Nihei...
- But Nihei provoked them, right?

269
00:18:59,859 --> 00:19:03,194
Yeah, but still...

270
00:19:11,853 --> 00:19:14,694
You're defending him an awful lot.

271
00:19:26,572 --> 00:19:28,720
Did you give him an answer?

272
00:19:29,532 --> 00:19:32,337
Huh? An answer?

273
00:19:35,492 --> 00:19:37,638
Of course I said no.

274
00:19:37,638 --> 00:19:40,965
And? Did he give up?

275
00:19:43,027 --> 00:19:46,758
He said he doesn't want to give up.

276
00:19:46,758 --> 00:19:48,291
But I'm not going to say yes.

277
00:19:48,291 --> 00:19:51,880
Because I'm with you, Kazumi.

278
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,787
Is that everything?

279
00:19:56,611 --> 00:20:00,462
What do you mean by, "Is that everything"?

280
00:20:00,462 --> 00:20:02,951
Are you hiding something?

281
00:20:03,737 --> 00:20:08,314
Sorry, I don't want to fight.

282
00:20:08,314 --> 00:20:11,328
Wait, don't brush me off.

283
00:20:11,328 --> 00:20:13,569
I'm telling you the truth.

284
00:20:13,569 --> 00:20:15,808
There's nothing between us.

285
00:20:23,693 --> 00:20:28,572
Don't you trust me?

286
00:20:31,946 --> 00:20:36,972
Sorry, it's not that I don't trust you.

287
00:20:36,972 --> 00:20:41,694
It's okay. You don't need to change, Himari.

288
00:20:47,922 --> 00:20:49,801
Why are you smiling?

289
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:52,137
Huh?

290
00:20:55,164 --> 00:20:57,518
You won't answer me, huh?

291
00:21:00,628 --> 00:21:02,127
You know,

292
00:21:02,127 --> 00:21:06,134
I feel like I understood you better
when we were just friends.

293
00:21:18,268 --> 00:21:22,864
Then should we go back to being friends?

294
00:21:28,072 --> 00:21:31,451
If that's what you want, I'll do it.

295
00:21:34,454 --> 00:21:37,057
Why would you say that?

296
00:21:41,137 --> 00:21:44,506
Sorry, I think I should go home now.

297
00:21:57,074 --> 00:21:59,776
<i>What did I do wrong?</i>

298
00:22:02,853 --> 00:22:08,076
<i>Back when we were friends,
and now that we're lovers...</i>

299
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:14,666
<i>all I wanted was for her to smile.</i>

300
00:22:17,651 --> 00:22:20,684
<i>That should have been enough.</i>

301
00:22:26,301 --> 00:22:30,348
<i>But by becoming her lover,
I'm taking that away.</i>

302
00:22:33,582 --> 00:22:36,575
<i>Was there even a point to becoming lovers?</i>

303
00:22:41,265 --> 00:22:45,876
- Excuse me, are you okay?
- No, I'm the one who should be sorry.

304
00:22:51,153 --> 00:22:55,639
Are you perhaps Kazumi Hojo's friend?

305
00:22:55,639 --> 00:22:56,970
Huh?

306
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:49,490
I lost my lover and my best friend.

307
00:23:49,490 --> 00:23:53,259
I can't make anyone happy.

308
00:23:53,259 --> 00:23:57,440
I always wanted to come here
with the person I love.

309
00:23:57,440 --> 00:24:00,240
What am I even doing?
